  "binsNote": "Post-validation revision 8 (M1 step 5): class cells use zone7 (zone6 with the red zone split at the 10 and the 15 and the own 10 at the 5) then zoneR, then zone3; pools use ydlP (bands 1-2, 3-5, 6-10, 11-15, 16-20, then 10 yards, then 81-85, 86-90, 91-95 and 96-99 at the own end). A pooled play's touchdown flag counts only when it was drawn from this spot's own band. Before, a pool band 1-10 and a red-zone cell 6-20 let a play that scored from the 2 score from the 9, and a 10-yard-plus class always score from the 6-10."
